  "title": "review: fix round 1 (review): S3d cache-aware handoff economics: cached context retained or lost, uncached reconstructio",
  "spec": "Fix round 1 for T-1146: review T-1177 requested changes. fix round 1: address review T-1177 comment orchestrator/handoff_scorecard.py:382 [med]: format_report(card) previously returned json.dumps(card, indent=1), which included by_start, recommendations, and planner_handoffs alongside the new handoffs data. This diff replaces it with a tab-separated table that only renders the handoffs rows/medians, silently dropping by_start, recommendations, and planner_handoffs from the non-JSON (default) CLI text output of `orchestrator scorecard --han fix round 1 rule: handoff_scorecard.format_report keeps the previous text output (by_start, recommendations, planner_handoffs) and appends the new handoffs table and medians below it, so scorecard --handoffs loses nothing in text mode; add a test that the text report still contains the by_start and recommendations sections and the new table. Run .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh . until it exits 0; do not ask questions; report files changed and failures-only output.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1179"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_handoff_scorecard.py::test_handoff_cache_fields_and_effective_cost_from_synthetic_runs",
    "tests/test_handoff_scorecard.py::test_duplicated_evidence_and_latency",
    "tests/test_cli.py::test_scorecard_handoffs_shows_cache_columns",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh exits 0",
    "fix round 1: address review T-1177 comment orchestrator/handoff_scorecard.py:382 [med]: format_report(card) previously returned json.dumps(card, indent=1), which included by_start, recommendations, and planner_handoffs alongside the new handoffs data. This diff replaces it with a tab-separated table that only renders the handoffs rows/medians, silently dropping by_start, recommendations, and planner_handoffs from the non-JSON (default) CLI text output of `orchestrator scorecard --han",
    "fix round 1 rule: handoff_scorecard.format_report keeps the previous text output (by_start, recommendations, planner_handoffs) and appends the new handoffs table and medians below it, so scorecard --handoffs loses nothing in text mode; add a test that the text report still contains the by_start and recommendations sections and the new table."
  ],
