  "result": {
    "summary": "I checked the fix round against its acceptance. The text report keeps the legacy sections and appends the handoffs table and medians. The change reads sound and stays in scope. I did not run the test suite.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/handoff_scorecard.py",
        "line": 388,
        "issue": "format_report now prints the legacy JSON (by_start, recommendations, planner_handoffs) and appends the tab-separated handoffs table and per-kind medians. This meets the fix-round rule. The test at tests/test_cli.py:136 covers the by_start and recommendations sections. Duplicated evidence ids are joined with commas, so an id containing a comma or tab would make the row ambiguous. Low impact.",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/cli.py",
        "line": 643,
        "issue": "The scorecard --handoffs path now reads from a.root when given, matching the memory and cache modes. This is a small scope-adjacent change. It only affects which state directory is read and does not widen access beyond what other modes already allow.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
